    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0431" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 4/10–345: Circular
                    telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Diplomatic
                        Representatives in the American Republics </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-03T15:00:00-05:00">October 3, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my press statement on Argentine situation telegraphed
                        today<anchor n="35" xml:id="d289-f1"/> please discuss as soon as possible
                    with Foreign Minister of country to which you are accredited (except in the case
                    of Argentina) the question of consultation about the Argentine situation.</p>
                <p>Dept believes such consultation necessary because of failure of present Argentine
                    Government to fulfill obligations it undertook, at invitation of other American
                    republics, by its signature of Mexico City resolutions. Dept also believes
                    consultation might be best carried out through diplomatic channels.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph views of Foreign Minister regarding necessity for consultation
                    and method preferred.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For documentation regarding Uruguayan proposal in response to this U. S.
                        initiative, see <ref target="#pg185">page 185</ref> ff.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
